course: dictionary
lesson: 6349
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning fits. The word move is a good example. «In a flood, move up to higher floors and never walk in floodwater.» Here move means go from one place to another, like climbing up the stairs.
explain: Move can also be a noun: a turn or step in a game, or a smart action. «A moving swing is heavy and fast at a child's head height, so walk wide around swings.» Here moving means being in motion, so the swing is going back and forth. Ask yourself: is something being carried, is it a game, or is it about feelings?
explain: Move can also make someone feel something. If a film moves you, it touches your heart and may make you sad or happy. Phrases like «get a move on» (hurry up) and «move on» (go forward to the next thing) are also useful to learn as whole chunks.
fact: Move is a verb (move, moves, moved, moving) and it can also be a noun: a move.
fact: To move means to go from one place to another, or to change position.
fact: To move something means to carry or push it to another place.
fact: A move is a turn or step in a game, or a smart action, as in «a smart move».
fact: «Get a move on» means hurry up, and «on the move» means travelling or going somewhere.
exercise: «In a flood, move up to higher floors.» What does move mean here? | A turn in a game | Carry it away with the water | Make someone feel sad | *Go from one place to another
exercise: «That was a smart move in the chess game.» What is a move here? | *A turn or step in a game | A new home | Someone who carries things | A feeling of sadness
exercise: The film really moved Nadia, and she cried. What does moved mean? | Hurried her along | Pushed her out of the cinema | *Made her feel strong feelings | Carried her to another room
test: Jayden says «get a move on» means slow down. What does it really mean? | *Hurry up | Stop and rest | Turn around | Move house
test: Ella's family will move house next month. What does «move house» mean? | *Go and live in a new home | Push the table across the room | Carry the sofa to the garden | Make a smart move in a game
exam: «A moving swing is heavy and fast at a child's head height, so walk wide around swings.» What does moving mean here? | Feeling very sad | Lying still on the ground | Being carried to school | *Going back and forth in motion
